<title>CANADA: Ag Canada updates 1997/98 grain and oilseed S &amp; Ds.</title>
<headline>Ag Canada updates 1997/98 grain and oilseed S &amp; Ds.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Canada on Monday</p>
<p>updated its supply and demand estimates in grains and oilseeds</p>
<p>for crop year 1997/98 (Aug/July).</p>
<p>CROP   HARVEST  YIELD  OUTPUT  SUPPLY  EXPORT  CARRYOUT  PRICE</p>
<p>Durum ('000 ha) (T/ha)   -- thousands of metric tonnes  (C$/T)</p>
<p>1995/6  2,125   2.188  4,648   6,116   3,222   1,978     C$286</p>
<p>1996/7  2,096   2.243  4,703   6,686   4,000   1,700 C$204-224</p>
<p>1997/8  2,133   2.220  4,735   6,440   3,700   1,800 C$175-205</p>
<p>Wheat</p>
<p>1995/6  9,017   2.259 20,369  24,601  12,976   4,666     C$254</p>
<p>1996/7 10,556   2.443 25,792  30,558  15,500   7,700 C$193-208</p>
<p>1997/8  9,520   2.341 22,290  30,010  16,800   6,000 C$160-190</p>
<p>Barley</p>
<p>1995/6  4,365   2.986 13,035  14,866   2,826   1,749     C$170</p>
<p>1996/7  4,928   3.229 15,912  17,871   3,800   3,301 C$125-145</p>
<p>1997/8  4,340   3.111 13,500  16,810   3,500   2,450 C$110-140</p>
<p>Canola</p>
<p>1995/6  5,273   1.221  6,436   7,123   2,804     925     C$433</p>
<p>1996/7  3,479   1.448  5,037   6,082   2,375     505 C$440-460</p>
<p>1997/8  5,300   1.321  7,000   7,535   2,950     735 C$390-430</p>
<p>Flax</p>
<p>1995/6    860   1.285  1,105   1,207     842     172     C$433</p>
<p>1996/7    590   1.458    860   1,033     700     125 C$365-385</p>
<p>1997/8    746   1.361  1,015   1,141     760     161 C$320-360</p>
<p>N.B.:crop year average prices: No1 CWRS wheat and No1 CWAD (durum) based on Canadian Wheat Board producer final price I/S St. Lawrence/Vancouver; barley No1 Feed, Winnipeg Commodity Exchange cash I/S Vancouver; canola No1 Canada, WCE cash I/S Vancouver; flax No1 Canada Western WCE cash I/S Thunder Bay. 1996/7 and 1997/8 tonnage forecasts based on Agriculture Canada and Statistics Canada.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
